-- title:
--   Easy inequality of the Wiles–Lenstra numerical criterion
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a principal ideal ring, and let $R$ and $T$ be commutative $\mathcal O$-algebras. Let $\varphi\colon R \to T$ be a homomorphism of $\mathcal O$-algebras which is surjective as a map of sets, and let $\pi_R\colon R \to \mathcal O$ and $\pi_T\colon T \to \mathcal O$ be $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms (augmentations) such that $\pi_T \circ \varphi = \pi_R$. Assume that the ideal $\ker \pi_R \subseteq R$ is finitely generated. Write $\eta_T$ for the ideal of $\mathcal O$ generated by the image under $\pi_T$ of the annihilator $\operatorname{Ann}_T(\ker \pi_T)$, and $\Phi_R = \ker\pi_R / (\ker\pi_R)^2$ for the cotangent module of the ideal $\ker\pi_R$. Then the length of $\mathcal O/\eta_T$ as an $\mathcal O$-module is at most the length of $\Phi_R$ as an $\mathcal O$-module, both lengths being taken in $\mathbb N \cup \{\infty\}$. No finiteness, locality, flatness or completeness hypothesis on $R$ or $T$ is imposed beyond finite generation of $\ker\pi_R$.
--
--   This is the easy half of the Wiles–Lenstra numerical criterion for complete intersections, comparing the congruence ideal of the augmented algebra $T$ with the cotangent module of the augmented algebra $R$ mapping onto it. It is used in the form of the criterion that converts an inequality of lengths into bijectivity of $\varphi$ ([`AlgHom.bijective_and_torsionBySet_eq_smul_of_length_le`](thm.html#AlgHom.bijective_and_torsionBySet_eq_smul_of_length_le)), and in the computation of cotangent lengths from presentations ([`AlgHom.length_cotangent_eq_of_exists_presentation`](thm.html#AlgHom.length_cotangent_eq_of_exists_presentation)).
